<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $1.6 bln in March 17 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $1.6 bln in March 17 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.6 billion in the March 17 week to $3,876.9 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $300 million to $5,008.7 billion. M-1 fell $5.2 billion to $1,072.3 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,873.0 billion versus $3,870.7 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
